{
  "id": "range-sum-query-immutable",
  "questionId": "range-sum-query-immutable",
  "slug": "range-sum-query-immutable",
  "title": "Range Sum Query - Immutable",
  "difficulty": "Easy",
  "category": "Prefix sum",
  "patterns": [
    "prefix sum"
  ],
  "lists": [],
  "hints": [
    "if the same array is queried many times, is there a way to avoid rescanning the range from scratch on every query?",
    "build a prefix sum array where prefix[i] holds the sum of nums[0..i-1]",
    "the sum of nums[left..right] inclusive is then prefix[right+1] - prefix[left]",
    "compute the prefix array once up front, then each query becomes a single subtraction"
  ],
  "commonMistakes": [
    "off-by-one when building the prefix array or when subtracting for an inclusive range",
    "recomputing the prefix sum for every query instead of once up front",
    "not handling left = 0 correctly (should just be prefix[right+1])"
  ],
  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You're given a fixed array of integers and a batch of range queries.\nEach query is a pair [left, right] (inclusive, 0-indexed).\n\n**For every query, compute the sum of the elements in that range, and return all the answers in the same order as the queries.**\n\nThe array never changes between queries, so precompute whatever helps answer many queries quickly.\n",
    "constraints": [
      "1 <= nums.length <= 10^4",
      "-10^5 <= nums[i] <= 10^5",
      "0 <= left <= right < nums.length",
      "0 <= queries.length <= 10^4"
    ],
    "notes": [
      "a query where left equals right (a single element)",
      "a query covering the entire array",
      "no queries at all"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "Arguments passed into solution function",
    "outputFormat": "Return output matching method signature",
